# 6. LEAD STATUS AND WORKFLOW

## 6.1 Recommended Lead Statuses

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| NEW | Lead has been created |
| UNDER_REVIEW | Admin is reviewing the lead |
| ASSIGNED | Lead has been assigned to a contractor |
| ACCEPTED | Contractor accepted the lead |
| CONTACTED | Contractor contacted the customer |
| SITE_VISIT_SCHEDULED | A site visit has been scheduled |
| QUOTE_IN_PROGRESS | Contractor is preparing a quotation |
| CONVERTED | Lead resulted in a confirmed business conversion |
| NOT_INTERESTED | Customer or contractor is not proceeding |
| CLOSED | Lead has been closed |
| CANCELLED | Lead has been cancelled |

These statuses represent suggested workflow states. Final business terminology and transition policies should be configurable or confirmed before implementation.

## 6.2 Lead Lifecycle

```text
CUSTOMER SUBMITS ENQUIRY
          |
          v
       NEW LEAD
          |
          v
     ADMIN REVIEW
          |
          +----------------------+
          |                      |
          v                      v
      ASSIGNED              NOT ELIGIBLE
          |                      |
          v                      v
   CONTRACTOR INBOX             CLOSED
          |
          v
       ACCEPTED
          |
          v
       CONTACTED
          |
          v
 SITE VISIT SCHEDULED
          |
          v
    QUOTE IN PROGRESS
          |
          +-----------------------+
          |                       |
          v                       v
      CONVERTED              NOT INTERESTED
          |                       |
          v                       v
        CLOSED                  CLOSED
```

The backend must enforce valid state transitions.

Do not allow contractors to change arbitrary lead statuses.

## 6.3 Assignment Rules

Only authorized administrators can assign or reassign leads.

Before assignment, the backend must verify:

1. Contractor exists.
2. Contractor account is active.
3. Contractor verification status is APPROVED.
4. Contractor is not suspended.
5. Contractor is eligible under platform rules.
6. Lead is in an assignable state.
7. Contractor is eligible for the lead's location and service requirements, when those rules are configured.

### Assignment Information

Every assignment must record:

- Lead ID
- Contractor ID
- Assigned By
- Assigned At
- Assignment Status
- Assignment Notes
- Previous Contractor ID, when reassigned

Never silently overwrite assignment history.

## 6.4 Reassignment

An administrator may reassign a lead when:

- Contractor rejects the lead.
- Contractor does not respond within an approved response period.
- Contractor becomes suspended.
- Contractor is unable to serve the location.
- Customer requests another contractor.
- Administrator identifies an operational reason.

The system must:

- Preserve the previous assignment.
- Record the reassignment reason.
- Record the new contractor.
- Update the current assignment.
- Create an audit record.
- Notify relevant users through the available notification system.

Response deadlines and automatic reassignment rules must not be invented. Keep them configurable until the business confirms the policy.

