# 7. CONTRACTOR LEAD MANAGEMENT

## 7.1 Contractor Dashboard

Approved contractors should have a dedicated lead management area.

Recommended dashboard sections:

- New Assigned Leads
- Accepted Leads
- Contacted Leads
- Site Visits
- Quotes in Progress
- Converted Leads
- Closed Leads

### Lead List Information

Each lead card or row should display:

- Lead Reference Number
- Customer Name
- Project Name
- Property City or Location Summary
- Deck Area
- Surface Type
- Enquiry Date
- Lead Status
- Related Estimate Reference
- Last Updated Date

Avoid exposing unnecessary customer personal information in list views.

## 7.2 Contractor Lead Details

When a contractor opens an assigned lead, the details page may display:

- Customer contact information needed to handle the enquiry.
- Property location.
- Deck information.
- Relevant photographs.
- Existing condition details.
- Related estimate snapshot.
- Customer enquiry message.
- Assignment information.
- Lead activity history.

Access must be restricted to the currently assigned contractor.

A contractor must not access another contractor's lead by modifying the URL or API request.

## 7.3 Contractor Actions

Depending on the current status, the contractor may:

- Accept the lead.
- Reject the lead with a reason.
- Mark the customer as contacted.
- Schedule a site visit.
- Update quotation progress.
- Mark the lead as converted.
- Mark the lead as not interested.
- Add an activity note.

All actions must be validated by the backend.

Contractors must not be allowed to:

- Change the customer ID.
- Change the deck ID.
- Change the lead owner.
- Change the assigned contractor ID.
- Modify assignment history.
- Modify administrative review information.
- Change the estimate's original calculation.

## 7.4 Lead Activity Timeline

Every important lead action should create an activity entry.

Examples:

- Lead created.
- Lead reviewed.
- Lead assigned.
- Assignment changed.
- Contractor accepted.
- Contractor rejected.
- Customer contacted.
- Site visit scheduled.
- Quote preparation started.
- Lead converted.
- Lead closed.
- Admin added a note.

Activity entries should include:

- Lead ID
- Actor ID
- Actor Role
- Activity Type
- Description
- Previous Status, if applicable
- New Status, if applicable
- Timestamp

Historical activity records should not be silently overwritten.

