# 15. AUTHORIZATION AND SECURITY

Security is a critical part of this phase.

The backend is the authority for all role, ownership, assignment, and status decisions.

## 15.1 Authentication

Reuse Phase 3 authentication middleware.

Do not create a second authentication system.

## 15.2 Role Authorization

Use the existing role system.

Required access categories:

- CUSTOMER
- CONTRACTOR
- ADMIN

Use existing role constants rather than introducing inconsistent role names.

## 15.3 Contractor Authorization

Before allowing contractor lead access, validate:

```text
Authenticated User
        |
        v
User Role = CONTRACTOR?
        |
        v
Account Active?
        |
        v
Verification Status = APPROVED?
        |
        v
Lead Assigned To This Contractor?
        |
        v
Allow Access
```

Every check must occur on the backend.

## 15.4 Lead Ownership

For customer access:

```text
lead.customerId === authenticatedUser.id
```

For contractor access:

```text
lead.assignedContractorId === authenticatedUser.id
```

Use the actual existing user-to-profile relationship when implementing these checks.

Do not assume a contractor profile ID and user ID are interchangeable.

## 15.5 Mass Assignment Protection

Never allow users to submit protected fields through generic updates.

Protected fields include:

- customerId
- assignedContractorId
- assignedBy
- verificationStatus
- approvedAt
- reviewedBy
- lead status outside permitted transitions
- assignment history
- audit information
- internal notes

Use explicit field allowlists.

## 15.6 Sensitive Information

Protect:

- Contractor verification documents.
- Customer phone numbers.
- Customer email addresses.
- Property addresses.
- Internal Admin notes.

Return only information necessary for the requesting role.

## 15.7 File Security

Use the secure upload practices established in Phase 4.

Validate actual file content, not just extensions.

Do not expose private files through unrestricted public storage paths.

